  "verbalization": "Gentiside K appears to have a shared target of CD276 antigen across multiple paths, with varying intermediate molecules leading to ME-180. The evidence suggests that Gentiside K may act through a series of metabolic or enzymatic pathways, ultimately targeting CD276 antigen, which in turn influences ME-180. The presence of multiple distinct intermediates—such as Prudomestin, 1-Hydroxy-7-methoxyxanthone, and (2R)-2-bromo-2-iodoacetic acid—indicates that the pathway may involve different biochemical mechanisms, possibly through distinct enzyme interactions or metabolic transformations. These variations in intermediates do not diminish the overall relationship between Gentiside K and ME-180, as all ultimately converge on CD276 antigen. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the interaction, with CD276 antigen serving as a central node in the network. The evidence supports a mechanism where Gentiside K modulates CD276 antigen, which then affects ME-180, though the exact nature of the interaction remains partially obscured by the diversity of intermediates.",
